WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.174
&gt;&gt;&gt; CNN has learned that former

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.375
president trump will huddle with

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.777
his legal team at mar-a-lago

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.345
this weekend as a potential

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:13.880
indictment looms over his

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.448
alleged role in hush-money

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.151
payments made to adult film star

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.285
stormy Daniels.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.553
A source tells CNN trump is

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.888
weighing whether to appear

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:22.722
before a New York grand jury

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:23.890
that's investigating the

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:24.791
payments that were made days

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.293
before the 2016 presidential

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:27.894
election.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.494
Manhattan prosecutors have

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.063
invited trump to appear.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.264
CNN senior legal analyst and

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.967
former federal and state

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.105
prosecutor Elly Hoenig joins me,

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:42.041
elii, I feel like when I read

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:45.111
the title of your book, it is a

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.046
perfect segue to our

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:47.480
conversations.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:48.948
What do you think trump will do?

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.550
He's not going to talk to the

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:50.950
grand jury.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.051
He's not going to do that.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.453
&gt;&gt; Absolutely not.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.020
No.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:54.754
N-o, no way.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.289
There would be no reason for him

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:57.123
to do that.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.458
This is an unusual feature of

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.192
New York state law.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.760
This isn't just the prosecutors

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.095
being nice and giving him a

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:02.929
chance to do this.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.731
They have to give any potential

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:05.999
defendant a chance to come in

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.500
and testify in the grand jury.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.901
That's actually not the law in

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:09.502
many states.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.471
That's certainly not the law

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:12.071
federally.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.606
There's no upside here.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.741
Donald Trump is not going to

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.942
talk a grand jury out of doing

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.143
whatever it might do.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:18.144
All he can do is give

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.213
information that can be used to

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:20.680
incriminate him.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.082
In this case or in many of the

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.083
other civil lawsuits and pending

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.318
criminal investigations against

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:25.585
him.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.053
So easy call for Donald Trump

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:27.353
here.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.688
Thank you for the invitation,

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.324
but I respectfully decline.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.091
&gt;&gt; We've been talking about the

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.626
stormy Daniels case for years

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.027
now.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.328
And you and I have talked about

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.063
it for years now, I feel like.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.966
Does that timeline matter

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:40.266
legally?

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.368
&gt;&gt; So legally it does not

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:42.702
matter.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.070
Some people have asked about the

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.271
statute of limitations which

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.439
usually is five years, meaning

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.474
you have to charge a case within

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.976
five years of when it ended.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.412
Here these payments happened 6.5

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:52.979
years ago.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:53.980
The thing is, New York

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.982
prosecutors are going to be okay

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.150
on that count because there's a

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.451
law in New York state that says

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.386
if somebody has been

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.587
continuously residing outside of

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.955
New York state, you put that

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:03.990
clock on hold.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.091
So they're well within the

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.025
statute of limitations.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.994
Jim, the amount of time that has

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.595
passed here is going to make

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:10.930
this prosecution more difficult

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.365
for the prosecutors because it's

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.000
harder to stand in front of a

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.201
jury and argue about something

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.103
that happened that long ago and

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.172
make them believe that it's

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.106
serious and urgent.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.008
To an extent the amount of time

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:22.942
that's passed is going to make

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.744
this a tougher job for

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:25.144
prosecutors.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.079
&gt;&gt; And trump's lawyers are

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:29.015
saying that this case is

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:29.449
unprecedented.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.250
I suppose that is the

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.218
understatement of the year.

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.821
Are they right?

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.122
&gt;&gt; They're right in hay couple

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:36.522
respects.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.623
First of all, of course if

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.458
there's an indictment we know

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.126
this would be the first-ever

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.327
indictment of a former

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:41.694
president.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:42.295
That would be historic.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.529
That would be unprecedented.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.597
But they're also right as a

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.799
matter of law because the theory

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.501
here that prosecutors appear to

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.702
be using is, first of all,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.137
they're going to charge it looks

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.638
like falsefications of business

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.440
records which is a misdemeanor,

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.042
meaning basically these were

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.044
hush-money payments, but they

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.178
falsely booked them as attorney

00:02:59.312 --> 00:02:59.479
fees.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:04.250
In order to bump it up to a

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:04.951
low-level felony prosecutors

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.052
have to prove it was connected

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:06.519
to some other crime.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.054
Here they will argue it was a

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:08.955
campaign finance crime relating

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.723
to the presidential election.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.325
What we don't know here is this

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.460
is a state-level prosecution,

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.394
the campaign finance violation

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.763
was federal, relating to the

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.931
race for president.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.000
And there's flow -- there's no

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.068
law on that.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.604
That will have to be decided by

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:24.937
a judge.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:25.638
That's unprecedented, as well.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.574
&gt;&gt; In your book you reveal the

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.643
southern district of New York

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.078
decided not to proceed two years

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:32.211
ago.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.079
Does that give insight into

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:35.148
what the outcome may be here?

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.183
&gt;&gt; Legally it does not matter.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.417
It doesn't mean that the

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.685
Manhattan D.A. Cannot prosecute

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:40.219
this case.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.255
They can come to a different

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.523
conclusion than the feds, my

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.391
former office across the street

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.493
did.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.094
Also we're dealing with

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:48.661
different sets of law.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.263
The Manhattan D.A. May have come

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.364
up with new evidence that the

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.832
feds didn't have two years ago.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.233
That said, I think it's

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.102
important, I think the Manhattan

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.104
D.A. Would be well advised to

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.472
consider the fed's logic.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:00.840
Look, the feds, when they looked

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:01.674
at the cases, the southern

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:02.742
district of New York, they

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.644
believed that the evidence was

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.646
sufficient to charge but not

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.413
overwhelming, and the southern

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.048
district of New York was wary

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.683
about the political factors.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.251
They were wary about the fact

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.321
that this felt, a, old, and, B,

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:16.989
fairly low on the list of

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:17.723
trump's misconduct.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.126
So this is a difficult call for

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:20.526
any prosecutor.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.128
There's no necessarily right or

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:22.595
wrong answer.

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:24.397
But I think the Manhattan D.A.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.132
Would be well advised to at

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.333
least look at what the thought

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:28.301
process was there.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.536
&gt;&gt; And aside from trump and

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.571
stormy Daniels, the other key

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.706
player is Michael Cohen, trump's

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.775
former fixer who's been very

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:36.642
critical, sharply critical of

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.144
the former president.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.011
Does that complicate things?

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.713
We all know Michael Cohen, we've

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:44.150
heard from Michael Cohen a lot.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.084
He was on this program last

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:45.384
week.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:46.652
He does not pull his punches

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.287
when it comes to his old boss.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.655
&gt;&gt; He does not.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.523
Michael Cohen looks like he's

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:52.158
going to be a pivotal witness in

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:52.692
this case.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.293
On the one hand.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.494
Michael Cohen clearly had

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.829
insider access, he was in the

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.164
middle of this transaction.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.699
He pled guilty to it, and many

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.033
of the things that Michael Cohen

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.269
has said since he did his prison

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:04.537
time about Donald Trump have

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:05.538
been proven out to be true.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.206
On the other hand, the reality

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.075
is like it or not, Michael Cohen

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.444
is going to be vulnerable to a

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.178
searing cross-examination.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.779
He has been convicted of

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:14.247
perjury.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.781
He has been convicted of tax

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:16.549
fraud and financial fraud.

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.751
He denies that he did it, but he

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:22.588
pled guilty to those crimes.

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:28.661
Michael cone has a white-hot

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:32.331
hard for Donald Trump.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.032
On cross-examination they're

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:35.334
going to argue this guy despises

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:36.502
druch, he'd do anything to --

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.071
Donald Trump, he'd do anything

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:39.472
to get him.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:40.406
Michael Cohen is going to be a

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:41.073
key witness here.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:42.275
I understand why one may want to

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.876
rest the case on him, I get

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.011
where prosecutors are going.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.679
But make no mistake, defense

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:47.780
liars are going to have a lot of

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.815
hay to make on

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:50.383
cross-examination.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.952
&gt;&gt; And of course just one of

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:54.921
several cases that may be on the

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.689
horizon for the former

